{{/*
  interaction-mode — the standard "Interaction Mode" block for prompts that
  can run either as an unattended scheduled loop OR as a normal on-demand
  conversation, WITHOUT any prompt-specific extras.

  This is the "sync-tasks style" flavor: the interactive branch phrases
  itself as "a regular conversation or a force-triggered loop run" and
  frames interactive tools as the default. Used by prompts where the
  primary mode is on-demand and the scheduled loop is opt-in.

  Consumers: jira/sync-tasks, jira/pull-issue, jira/push-issue,
  github/sync-tasks.

  For prompts whose primary mode is the scheduled loop (with on-demand as
  the force-triggered exception), use `_shared/interaction-mode-babysit`
  instead. For loop drivers marked "READ THIS FIRST", use
  `_shared/interaction-mode-unattended`.

  If your prompt needs extra bullets (autonomy criteria, stop-iterating
  hooks, references to specific steps), do NOT use this fragment —
  hand-roll the block using `_shared/silent-notify-only.tmpl` for the
  common preamble and add your own bullets around it.

  Usage:

    {{ template "_shared/interaction-mode" . }}

  The fragment emits its own `## Interaction Mode` heading — do NOT add
  one at the call site.
*/}}
## Interaction Mode
{{- if and .Session.IsLoop (not .Session.IsLoopForced) }}

**Silent mode** — a scheduled loop run; the user is not watching.
{{ template "_shared/silent-notify-only" . }}
{{- else }}

**Interactive mode** — a regular conversation or a force-triggered loop run; the user is present.
- Use interactive tools (`mitto_ui_options`, `mitto_ui_form`, `mitto_ui_textbox`) as well as `mitto_ui_notify`. This is the default when run on demand.
{{- end }}
